## Why This Is Asked
To assess hands-on Azure AI wiring for accessibility use cases, including voice input, multilingual output, and privacy controls, all grounded in a managed KB.

## Key Concepts
- Azure API Management as a gate
- Azure OpenAI with grounding to a versioned KB in Blob via Cognitive Search
- Azure Speech to Text and Text to Speech
- Per-tenant language preferences
- PII redaction and interaction logging

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example flow tying services together
async function handleQuery(audioBlob, language) {
  const text = await speechToText(audioBlob, language);
  const answer = await openai.chat({ messages: [{ role: 'user', content: text }] });
  const tts = await textToSpeech(answer.choices[0].message.content, language);
  return tts;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you model per-tenant language settings in Cosmos DB?
- What are the trade-offs between cloud TTS and on-device synthesis for accessibility tasks?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design end-to-end RAG pipelines with governance in a realistic Azure stack.

## Key Concepts
- Retrieval augmented generation, vector search, API Management, per-tenant residency, secret redaction, monitoring.
- Access controls, cost vs latency trade-offs, data provenance.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Redact secrets from user prompt
function redactPrompt(input){
  return input.replace(/(password|token|secret)\s*=\s*\S+/gi, '$1=REDACTED');
}
```

```javascript
// Simple guardrail stub: block disallowed topics in response
function guardResponse(text){
  const forbidden=[/internal-credential|secret-key/i];
  for(const f of forbidden){
    if(f.test(text)) return text.replace(f, 'REDACTED');
  }
  return text;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle index refresh cadence vs API latency in a large codebase?
- What metrics would you collect to detect degradation in retrieval quality?
